   "evidence": "grep for `isReal` across `EpsilonEridani/` returns only `isReal_iff`, `isReal_iff_norm_spatialPart_eq_energy` and `not_isReal_of_mem_photonRegion`; the `|a| = |v\u2070|` form exists only at the Lorentz level (`MinkowskiProductExtensions.lean:128`, about `\u27eav,v\u27eb\u2098 = 0`, not about `IsReal`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/Photoproduction/Kinematics/InvariantMass.lean",
   "fix": "Add to `Kinematics/Basic.lean` the collinear criterion `isReal_iff_abs_eq_energy_of_spatialPart_eq_smul (hn : \u2016n\u2016 = 1) (hq) (h\u03b3) (hk) (hq' : q.spatialPart = a \u2022 n) : \u03b3.IsReal \u2194 |a| = \u03b3.energy` (one rewrite from `Lorentz.Vector.minkowskiProduct_self_eq_zero_iff_of_spatialPart_eq_smul`), and the forward-cone corollary `q.spatialPart = \u03b3.energy \u2022 n` from `\u03b3.IsReal` and `0 \u2264 a`, then cite it in the docstrings at lines 35-39, 104 and 137.",
   "issue": "The module docstring claims \"a photon of momentum `a` along the beam axis is real exactly when `|a| = k`\" and cites `PhotonKinematics.isReal_iff_norm_spatialPart_eq_energy`, but that lemma only gives `\u2016q.spatialPart\u2016 = \u03b3.energy` (Kinematics/Basic.lean:103). No declaration states the collinear form, and nothing converts `\u03b3.IsReal` plus `q.spatialPart = a \u2022 n`, `0 \u2264 a` into `q.spatialPart = \u03b3.energy \u2022 n` \u2014 the hypothesis gating both headline theorems (lines 106 and 139), so the real-photon entry point to this module is unreachable without hand-rolled `norm_smul`/sign work.",
   "line": 35
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Rapidity.lean:93-99 is the only place the quotient appears; the file's direction lemma `rapidity_smul_right_of_pos` (line 108) covers positive rescaling of `n` only, and no lemma mentions `-v`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/Rapidity.lean",
   "fix": "Add the unconditional `rapidity_neg_left : (-v).rapidity n = v.rapidity n`, proved from `rapidity_def` with `neg_apply`/`inner_neg_left` and `neg_div_neg_eq`.",
   "issue": "The `rapidity` docstring (and the module docstring, line 27) asserts \"for a past-directed `v` with `|v_\u2225| < -v\u2070` it is the rapidity of `-v`\", i.e. `(-v).rapidity n = v.rapidity n`, but no lemma states it; a user wanting it must unfold `rapidity_def`.",
